{
    "m_SGVersion": 0,
    "m_Type": "UnityEditor.ShaderGraph.StickyNoteData",
    "m_ObjectId": "ebeb9c98c6cf45e982a500af04b55345",
    "m_Title": "Outline",
    "m_Content": "Draws glowing outlines on mesh faces\n\nHow it works:\r\n1/  GetCoordFromPosition turns each UV axis into a triangle wave (1 at edges, 0 at center).\r\n2/ edgeGradient = max(coord(u), coord(v)) → high near any face border.\r\n3/ Three additive layers build the look:\r\n         - Stroke step(0.99) → sharp line on the edge\r\n         - Glow pow(saturate((edgeGradient − GlowThreshold) × GlowSlop), GlowFallOff) → soft gradient fading inward\r\n         - Base fill + BaseFill → faint constant tint so the center is never fully transparent\r\n4/ _Color tints the result; the Back Face branch multiplies back-facing edges by BackFaceThreshold for a depth cue.\r\n\nTunable properties:\r\n- _Color : overall tint\r\n- GlowThreshold : where the glow starts (lower = wider gradient)\r\n- GlowSlop : glow slope/intensity (≈ 1 / (1 − GlowThreshold) to peak at the edge)\r\n- GlowFallOff : glow softness (lower = softer/wider)\r\n- BaseFill : constant fill, never fully transparent (≈ 0.15)\r\n- BackFaceThreshold : back-face dimming (1 = equal, 0.5 = slight depth cue) ",
    "m_TextSize": 0,
    "m_Theme": 0,
    "m_Position": {
        "serializedVersion": "2",
        "x": 1106.0,
        "y": -325.0,
        "width": 674.0,
        "height": 314.0
    },
    "m_Group": {
        "m_Id": ""
    }
}

